l_distance_km is null, the re-quote is missing from the record, the clause cannot be run, POL-RD-10(5) applies, and the Judge must not derive a substitute figure. POL-RD-10(5) names this very situation — 'a POL-RD-05 amendment with amended_optimal_distance_km null' — as a mandatory escalation trigger. I therefore cannot re-price the journey that was actually agreed (from the West Grove pickup to the endpoint as amended) and cannot determine what fare is properly chargeable for it. That is a defect in the record, not a finding for either party, and POL-RD-10 escalation is terminal. What would resolve it, and what the reviewer should obtain, is the platform's re-quote for the amended route: amended_optimal_distance_km and amended_optimal_duration_min for TRP-00714.\n\nTHE REMAINING POINTS. The rider's claim that she was billed for a drive she was not on fails under POL-RD-11, which fixes the upfront fare at booking and allows only an over-quote amount (0.00 here) or a POL-RD-09 pass-through correction (none here) — so that limb of her case is rejected on its merits. Her POL-RD-05 argument does not yield a refund either; it is the spring of the escalation, not a payment. The driver's points — no deviation (excess 0.0 km / 0%), upfront fare, no overcharge (charged_over_quote 0.00), no pass-through lines, no billing-integrity defect — are all accepted as far as they go, but none of them cures the missing amended re-quote that POL-RD-05 and POL-RD-10(5) require me to act on. EV-ADVIS-00714-01 is MISSING, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight_multiplier 0.0; no traffic advisory exists for this window, so no POL-RD-03 external-cause exoneration can be run and the driver's endpoint account supplies no amended optimal (POL-RD-13) — that absence is recorded but is not a second escalation ground. On the profile, EV-RPROF-00714 shows deviation_claims_60d = 0 and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated = 0, so the POL-RD-08 corroboration factor is not engaged and the rider's account has