    "explanation": "To both parties: this case goes to a human reviewer, and no money moves while it is there. The disputed SGD 16.80 is held — it is not collected from the rider and it is not paid to the driver.\n\nWhy it cannot be decided here. Your trip record (EV-TRIP-00714) shows the dropoff point was amended after booking: dropoff_amended_at is 2026-09-24T11:21:10, the same minute the rider messaged 'We are getting out here. End our booking at this stop' (EV-CHAT-00714, MSG-00714-002). But the amended optimal figures are null — amended_optimal_distance_km and amended_optimal_duration_min are both empty. POL-RD-05 says in terms that where an amendment timestamp is present but amended_optimal_distance_km is null, the re-quote is missing from the record, the clause cannot be run, and POL-RD-10(5) applies; the Judge must not derive a substitute figure. POL-RD-10(5) then makes escalation mandatory and terminal, so trigger (5) is what fired. What would resolve it is the platform's stored amended optimal distance and duration for the amended endpoints (or a corrected trip record); that is what the reviewer needs.\n\nWhat the rest of the evidence shows, so you both know where things sit. On EV-GPS-00714 the trace length is 10.8 km against the booked optimal of 10.8 km on EV-TRIP-00714 — an excess of 0.0 km and 0%. That is below both POL-RD-01 gates (0.8 km and 20% of optimal), so no route deviation is established on this trip. The fare is an upfront quote: EV-FARE-00714 shows fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE, quoted_fare_sgd 16.80 and total_charged 16.80, so under POL-RD-11 POL-RD-02 does not run and no distance-or-time refund is available; charged_over_quote is 0.00. Every pass-through and statutory line is zero — ERP 0.00, airport surcharge 0.00, waiting-time fee 0.00 — so POL-RD-09 has no off-route or phantom line and no surcharge to correct. The rider's early exit (her own device static at 0.0 kph from 11:21:10 on EV-GPS-00714, and her message on EV-CHAT-00714) does not by itself generate a distance refund on an upfront-paid fare. On those grounds alone the merits point to NO_ACTION; the mandatory escalation displaces that ruling because the record cannot be re-priced.\n\nThe missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00714-01 is not a second trigger. It is MISSING, carries issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT and weight 0.0, but no party asserted an external traffic cause, so POL-RD-03 was never invoked and POL-RD-13 does not engage.\n\nThe driver's in-app demand of SGD 15 for the second passenger (EV-CHAT-00714, MSG-00714-001) is not a line on the ledger — the fare breakdown contains no such charge — so there is nothing to refund for it, and with no repeat-deviation pattern on the driver's profile (deviation_flags_90d is 0) POL-RD-06 produces no conduct referral. That message is a matter the reviewer will see in the file, but no clause turns it into a monetary order on this record.\n\nNet position: escalate and hold the SGD 16.80. No refund and no driver compensation issue on the present record."
